NOT COMMITTED -- what `--camera-assets` points at
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are 15 MB of texture and would double the size of the repository, so
they are downloaded rather than vendored. All CC0.

  Environment lighting
    "Kloofendal 43d Clear (Pure Sky)", 2K HDR, by Andreas Mischok (Poly Haven)
    https://polyhaven.com/a/kloofendal_43d_clear_puresky
    https://dl.polyhaven.org/file/ph-assets/HDRIs/hdr/2k/kloofendal_43d_clear_puresky_2k.hdr

    A pure-sky HDRI, chosen over the probe's `construction_yard` because that
    one's backdrop contains real people and vehicles and they generated their
    own detections above the horizon. This one lights the site the same way
    and puts nothing in it.

  Ground material
    "Gravel", 2K JPG, by Dimitrios Savva (Poly Haven)
    https://polyhaven.com/a/gravel
    https://dl.polyhaven.org/file/ph-assets/Textures/jpg/2k/gravel/gravel_diff_2k.jpg
    https://dl.polyhaven.org/file/ph-assets/Textures/jpg/2k/gravel/gravel_rough_2k.jpg
    https://dl.polyhaven.org/file/ph-assets/Textures/jpg/2k/gravel/gravel_nor_gl_2k.jpg

  Renderer
    Blender 5.2.1 LTS, Cycles, via the official `bpy` PyPI module (GPL-3.0),
    run as a subprocess -- see cycles.py for why it is not a dependency.
